<title>FRANCE: SCOR supported by SAFR deal.</title>
<headline>SCOR supported by SAFR deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in re-insurance group SCOR gained 4.66 percent to 236 francs at 0944 GMT as investors were adjusting the share's valuation following Wednesday's SAFR deal, dealers said.</p>
<p>AGF on Wednesday agreed to sell its 47 percent stake in Societe Anonyme de Reassurances (SAFR) for 2.5 billion francs to Swiss Re.</p>
<p>Scor shares have been rising quickly, with the market, from 181.20 francs on January 13. The share capital of the re-insurer has been fragmented after key shareholder AXA-UAP sold a stake on January 31.</p>
<p>Templeton Global Investors has more than five percent of the share capital of Scor since February 7.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
